      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The database is persistently inaccessible (authentication error on every attempt, including `SELECT 1`). I'll complete the analysis based on semantic-network evidence and the strong precedent metrics, then make one final verification attempt before submitting.\n\n---\n\n## Report\n\n### 1. Entity Semantics\n\n**Tables (gold set):**\n- **SIS_SUBJECT_CODE**: subject code lookup mapping subject codes/course numbers to descriptions, departments, schools. Key columns: `DEPARTMENT_CODE` (joins CIS_COURSE_CATALOG.DEPARTMENT_CODE and SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE), `DEPARTMENT_NAME`, `SCHOOL_NAME`. Granularity: one row per subject code/course number.\n- **CIS_COURSE_CATALOG**: alternative course catalog feed with unit structure. Key column: `TOTAL_UNITS` (total credit units), `DEPARTMENT_CODE`. Granularity: one row per subject per term.\n- **SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION**: catalog course descriptions. Key columns: `COURSE_DESCRIPTION`, `COURSE_LEVEL` ('U'/'G'), `DEPARTMENT` (joins SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE), `DEPARTMENT_NAME`.\n- **SIS_DEPARTMENT**: department dimension. Key columns: `DEPARTMENT_CODE`, `DEPARTMENT_NAME` (e.g. 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci'), `SCHOOL_NAME`.\n- **MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY**: one row per student. Key columns: `FULL_NAME`, `EMAIL_ADDRESS`, `STUDENT_YEAR`, `DEPARTMENT` (academic department code, joins SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE), `DEPARTMENT_NAME`.\n\n**Tables (related, investigated, not used):** STUDENT_DEPARTMENT (lighter department lookup, lacks degree-granting flag; SIS_DEPARTMENT preferred per concept decision guide), COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED / DRUPAL_COURSE_CATALOG (alternative catalog feeds with TOTAL_UNITS; the hint explicitly maps \"maximum total units\" to CIS_COURSE_CATALOG.TOTAL_UNITS), SUBJECT_SUMMARY / SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY / SUBJECT_OFFERED (registrar offering facts, not needed since no enrollment/term scope is asked).\n\n**Metrics (precedents):** dw_3969, dw_4458, dw_1474, dw_2240, dw_1983 — all contain the identical EECS-student subquery shape.\n\n**Concepts:** concept_department_dimension, concept_person_directory, concept_course_catalog_sources, concept_subject_offering_facts.\n**Column concepts:** column_concept_department_name, column_concept_total_units.\n\n### 2. Lineage & Relationships\n- Graph on CIS_COURSE_CATALOG: joins ↔ SIS_SUBJECT_CODE (via DEPARTMENT_CODE), SIS_DEPARTMENT, COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED; member of concept_course_catalog_sources; column member of column_concept_total_units.\n- Graph on MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY: joins ← SIS_DEPARTMENT (DEPARTMENT = DEPARTMENT_CODE), SE_PERSON (name-based); member of concept_person_directory.\n- Lineage of dw_3969 confirms the EECS pattern: `SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION t0 JOIN SIS_DEPARTMENT t1 ON t0.DEPARTMENT = t1.DEPARTMENT_CODE JOIN MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY t2 ON t1.DEPARTMENT_CODE = t2.DEPARTMENT WHERE t1.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci'`.\n\n### 3. Similar-Entity Differences\n- **TOTAL_UNITS sources** (column_concept_total_units): COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_SUMMARY, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY, CIS_COURSE_CATALOG, DRUPAL_COURSE_CATALOG all carry it. Task-hint anchoring: \"maximum total units: CIS_COURSE_CATALOG.TOTAL_UNITS\" and join key \"CIS_COURSE_CATALOG.DEPARTMENT_CODE ↔ SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.DEPARTMENT_CODE\" — the task lexically pins CIS_COURSE_CATALOG. Precedent dw_2210 also uses CIS_COURSE_CATALOG for catalog unit stats.\n- **DEPARTMENT_NAME sources**: SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.DEPARTMENT_NAME and SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME share the academic name domain (column_concept_department_name); hint maps \"department name\" to both — subq1 uses SIS_SUBJECT_CODE's (grouping side), subq2 uses SIS_DEPARTMENT's (filter side, per all 5 precedents).\n- **Student population**: only MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY covers students (concept_person_directory decision guide: \"Counting students belonging to an academic department → MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY joined to SIS_DEPARTMENT on DEPARTMENT = DEPARTMENT_CODE\").\n\n### 4. Business Usage\nFive precedent metrics (dw_3969, dw_4458, dw_1474, dw_2240, dw_1983) use the exact EECS student+course-description join shape; dw_2240 computes MAX(TOTAL_UNITS) per department over catalog subjects — the same \"max units per department\" task shape.\n\n### 5. Coverage Checklist\nAll Phase 1 entities investigated via semantic_get (5 gold tables, STUDENT_DEPARTMENT, COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, 5 precedent metrics, 4 concepts, 2 column concepts) and semantic_graph (CIS_COURSE_CATALOG neighbors, MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY neighbors, dw_3969 lineage). mysql_query attempted 9 times — all failed with `Access denied for user 'root'@'localhost'`, so data-level verification was impossible; the SQL follows verified precedent patterns exactly.\n\n### 6. Recommendation\n- **subq1**: `CIS_COURSE_CATALOG JOIN SIS_SUBJECT_CODE ON DEPARTMENT_CODE`, GROUP BY DEPARTMENT_NAME, SCHOOL_NAME, `HAVING MAX(TOTAL_UNITS) > 6` (fan-out from many subject codes per department is harmless under MAX).\n- **subq2**: precedent EECS pattern (SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION → SIS_DEPARTMENT → MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY, filter `DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci'`).\n- **Most common student year per course level**: mode via `ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY COURSE_LEVEL ORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC)` over (COURSE_LEVEL, STUDENT_YEAR) groups of subq2, keeping rn = 1.\n- Join subq1 ↔ subq2 on DEPARTMENT_NAME (same academic name domain), attach the mode year per COURSE_LEVEL. SELECT list exactly matches the 8 requested columns in order.\n\n",
